# Scroll-to-Top Button

When page content is taller than the viewport and the user has scrolled below the top:

- Show an **up arrow** in the **bottom-right corner** of the viewport.
- Clicking it **scrolls the page to the top**.
- The button should only appear when the user has scrolled down (e.g. past a small threshold like 100px).
- Use a fixed position so it stays in the corner while scrolling.

The `ScrollToTop` component is rendered once in the root layout (`app/layout.tsx`), so it appears on every page automatically. Do not import or add it to individual page components.
